    "cargo": "analista",
    "tipo": "multipla_escolha",
    "enunciado": "Considere o seguinte texto: \n\nNowadays, firewalls are way more sophisticated than they used to be. They are now capable of inspecting the application-level protocols and are often not only deployed at the forefront of the infrastructure but also between each component, to monitor and limit unauthorized accesses. \n\nFor the same reason, some container orchestrator tools (such as ......<sup>_I_</sup> , but also the public cloud providers) offer the possibility to implement the socalled network policies, which are essentially _II_ acting as a network ...... firewall, hence not allowing (or dropping) unwanted network connections. Firewalls can be hardware appliances (with major vendors including Cisco and Check Point, among others), or even software distributions (such as PFSense and Zeroshell). \n\n(Adaptado de: BONOCORE, Giuseppe. Hands-On Software Architecture with Java. Packt Publishing, 2022) \n\nAs lacunas I e II devem ser preenchidas, correta e respectivamente, com",
    "alternativas": [
      "Kubernetes e Access Control Lists",
      "Docker e Reverse Proxies",
      "Rancher e Disaster Recovery Policies",
      "Jenkins e Reverse Proxies",
      "Maven e Access Control Lists"
    ],
    "correta": 0,
    "trechoFonte": "Alocação contígua: partições fixas/variáveis → fragmentação externa (buracos entre blocos) e interna (sobra dentro do bloco). Estratégias: first-fit, best-fit, worst-fit.",
    "dificuldade": 3,
    "isBossStyle": true,
    "isRealExam": true,
    "banca": "FCC",
